Z||000012||Monkeyman||09-26-2001||08:20 PM||||I was just thinking as I listen to Cliffs chart topper (for the millionth time--Gawd, I love that tune), there must be a way to get some real sound into a phone.  Half of the ringtones are impossible to decipher.  (They're supposed to sound like what song??)  I realize that you're never going to get concert hall sound quality out of a cell phone, but there must be some way of changing the beeps to real sound.  Anyone know what could be done?  Could you incorporate an MP3 player into a phone?  I realize that the "music" is only to let you know that you have a call, not for my listening pleasure, but...||||reg||1
